---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LAUNCH_STATES } from '../data/states';
import { getStreams, getStockingEvents } from '../data/load';
import { websiteLd } from '../lib/seo';

const tn = LAUNCH_STATES[0];
const streams = getStreams(tn.id);
const events = getStockingEvents(tn.id);

const title =
  'Trout — match the hatch & stream conditions, offline. Free, no accounts, no tracking.';
const description =
  'The on-the-water decision tool for trout anglers: identify the bug, check fishability, and see Tennessee stocking schedules — all offline, with zero location tracking. Free.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/" ld={[websiteLd()]}>
  <p class="kicker">The on-the-water decision tool</p>
  <h1>Match the hatch. Check the water. Leave no trace of yourself.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Trout is a free web app for trout anglers that works where there's no signal and doesn't want
    your data. Identify the bug that's hatching, see whether the water is fishable, and know what
    got stocked — all computed on <em>your</em> device.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/install/"><strong>Add it to your home screen</strong></a> — no app store, no account,
    no download bigger than a photo album.
  </p>

  <h2>Three questions, answered before you make a cast</h2>
  <h3>1. What is this bug? (offline)</h3>
  <p>
    Work the structured ID key — size, color, tails, gills, shape — and get ranked insect matches
    with the fly patterns that imitate them, plus a 12-month hatch chart for your region. The whole
    key runs on your phone in airplane mode; no photo needed, no AI, no network.
  </p>
  <h3>2. Is this water fishable right now?</h3>
  <p>
    Live USGS gauge readings are scored 0–100 with plain-English reasons — no chart-reading
    homework. {streams.length} Tennessee streams are in the v1 catalog, each with ideal-flow ranges,
    the hatch chart for its region, and links to verify everything officially.
  </p>
  <h3>3. What got stocked, and when?</h3>
  <p>
    {events.length} TWRA stocking events are already mirrored on this site —{' '}
    <a href="/stocking/tn/">see the Tennessee stocking page</a>, and the app refreshes the weekly
    schedule when you have signal.
  </p>

  <h2>Honest positioning — what this is, and what it isn't</h2>
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Tool</th>
        <th scope="col">Its job</th>
        <th scope="col">Trout's difference</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Fishbrain</td>
        <td>Community &amp; social fishing log</td>
        <td>
          No feed, no social. The logbook lives only in your browser — never on a server.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>TroutRoutes</td>
        <td>Navigation, access &amp; land data</td>
        <td>
          Not a map. Trout answers "should I fish here right now, and with what?" — not "how do I
          get there?"
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>State agency sites</td>
        <td>Authoritative schedules &amp; regs</td>
        <td>
          We're the convenience layer, never the authority — every number links back to the official
          source.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Privacy by architecture, not by policy</h2>
  <p>
    There are no accounts in v1. Your location is computed on your device and is never sent
    anywhere. There is no third-party analytics in the app or on this site — the app works fully in
    airplane mode, which is the strongest privacy policy there is. Read{' '}
    <a href="/privacy/">the plain-English privacy page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Free to use</h2>
  <p>
    The app and this site are free. No paywall on hatch data, conditions, or stocking. Later
    versions may add clearly-labeled optional extras (alerts, a Pro tier) — the core decision tools
    stay free (see <a href="/blog/">launch notes</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>Start here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/install/">Install the app</a> on iOS, Android, or desktop</li>
    <li><a href="/stocking/tn/">Tennessee stocking schedule</a> (verify officially)</li>
    <li><a href="/streams/tn/south-holston-river/">Example stream page: South Holston River</a></li>
    <li><a href="/hatch/tn/east-holston-tailwaters/">East Tennessee hatch chart</a></li>
    <li><a href="/when-does-tennessee-stock-trout/">When does Tennessee stock trout?</a></li>
  </ul>
</Base>
